# "Enchant land": the Aura cannot be cast on a creature (the refusal), but can on any land, an opponent's included (the positive
# control). Enchanted land has the ability, so the land's controller - Bot2 - taps its Island for it: the Aura belongs to Bot1,
# the ability to whoever controls the land (CR 303.4e), and Bot2's Ornithopter gains trample and haste.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Footfall Crater
Mountain x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Ornithopter
Island x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Footfall Crater.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Hand.Footfall Crater.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Island)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate(Ornithopter; Ability: trample)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Footfall Crater.AttachedTo = Island
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying; Haste; Trample
